{
  "id": "metals_and_alloys___bulk_modulus_elasticity",
  "title": "Metals and Alloys - Bulk Modulus Elasticity",
  "description": "The Bulk Modulus - resistance to uniform compression - for common metals and alloys. This tool provides reference values and allows calculation of bulk modulus using the relationship with modulus of elasticity and Poisson's ratio.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Bulk Modulus Elasticity\n\nThe Bulk Modulus Elasticity - or Volume Modulus - is a measure of the substance's resistance to uniform compression. It is the ratio of stress to the change in volume in a material subjected to axial loading.\n\n### Relationship Formula\n\nBulk Modulus is related to Modulus of Elasticity and Poisson's Ratio as:\n\n**K = E / 3 (1 - 2r)**\n\nWhere:\n- **K** = Bulk Modulus (Pa or psi)\n- **E** = Modulus of Elasticity (Pa or psi)\n- **r** = Poisson's Ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "modulus_elasticity",
          "label": "Modulus of Elasticity (E)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 200,
          "unit": "GPa"
        },
        {
          "id": "poissons_ratio",
          "label": "Poisson's Ratio (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.3,
          "unit": ""
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "bulk_modulus",
          "label": "Bulk Modulus (K)",
          "formula": "inputs.modulus_elasticity / (3 * (1 - 2 * inputs.poissons_ratio))",
          "unit": "GPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
